# Gitleaks fingerprints for findings that are not secrets.
#
# Each entry is `<commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>` as printed in the gitleaks
# report. Keep this list empty of anything that was ever a real credential: a
# line belongs here only when the matching text is provably not a secret, and
# the justification says why. Do not quote the matched text in a comment — the
# scanner reads this file too, and a quoted literal of sufficient entropy gets
# reported as a new finding.

# The hex character set a Session token is validated against, passed to
# strings.Trim. generic-api-key matches it on entropy alone; it is a charset,
# not a credential.
